{"author":{"id":"fb9734b7331903226ef3f5df545b960dd5ac64d18b49faee11e8b8e0bd561c91"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1783542814,"nonce":"+fmrLrH+cHIBtrq69BwjLsOmLsg=","message":"Register-mechanism + budget-correctness work landed 2026-07-08; sampling arena validated end-to-end on the real 768px fp8 Krea2 smoke (exit 0, no non_pinned_pack). Full suite 328 green. Five bugs beyond the Phase 2 budget delta were fixed: (1) pin_alloc's caching-host-allocator power-of-two bucket rounding inflated 8.86 GiB of flats to 12.70 GiB of DXGI usage -\u003e new pin_manager.pin_register (cudaHostRegister on a page-exclusive carved buffer; exact DXGI cost, budget returned immediately on release); arena flats now pin via pin_mechanism='register'. (2) torch is_pinned() is blind to cudaHostRegister (only tracks its own caching-allocator pins) -\u003e pin_manager.is_host_pinned (is_pinned OR registration table), threaded into pack_block_host_from_flat and _fetch_start_impl. (3) the 'desired - committed' delta request undercounts per-leaf 256B alignment + 4096B register page-padding and forced marginal blocks pageable -\u003e attach now requests full desired and hands _build_pinned_arena the plan's usable weight headroom (headroom - reserve - bounce); build only rebuilds stale/pageable groups so it can't over-pin, pin_register enforces the true per-block limit. (4) bounce_reserve is now 0 when the arena is active (pinned weights bypass bounce staging, so reserving a bounce window for the same weights double-counted and clipped the arena below the streamed set). (5) _build_pinned_arena(priority_ids=selected_offload_ids) orders streamed blocks first + self-heals pageable-but-current blocks when budget recovers. Result: every attach pins the full streamed set (pageable_blocks=0, 9.92-\u003e10.87 GiB across the train-\u003esample growth), all 18 streamed ingraph packs BORROW the arena flats. Cleanup: _LIVE_ARENAS is a strong set with release() discard + a tests/conftest.py sweep (a GC'd arena fre